#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# chebyshev_t

#% text
# `chebyshev_t(n, x)` gives the Chebyshev polynomial of the first kind T_n(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% item
# T_n(cos t) = cos(n t).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
chebyshev_t(3, x)
#% output
#= -3*x + 4*x^3

#% cell
chebyshev_t(3, 0.3)
#% output
#= -0.792

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
chebyshev_t(0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.8062257748298549

#% cell
chebyshev_t(-2, x)
#% output
#= -1 + 2*x^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `chebyshev_u`, `legendre_p`
